    "body": "tengok 0.3.9: peek into any file. MIDI songs show their summary, instruments and a piano roll and play on the phone's built-in synth; images zoom; audio plays; text reads; everything else opens in a paged hex view with a details sheet (type, size, SHA-256). Offline, no accounts, zero Android permissions, files never leave the phone.\n\nGame mode turns any MIDI song into falling notes you can tap on an on-screen piano or play on a USB MIDI keyboard. Velocity and human timing stay as played, with no snapping. Scores and the diagnostic log stay on the phone; sharing a crash or diagnostics is always your tap.\n\n0.3.2 makes the on-screen piano playable on a phone: keys keep a finger-sized minimum width and the board pans by itself to keep the next notes in view; drag sideways on the keys to look around without striking. A tap still grades at the instant the finger lands. A live letter rank (D up to SSS, from accuracy plus your streak, so a miss pulls it down) shows in the lane while you play and as the final grade. The home screen keeps a recent-files list so a file opened once is one tap away: removing an entry only clears the list, the file itself is never touched, and reopening uses the access Android already granted. Still offline, still zero Android permissions.\n\n0.3.9 finishes the glide work from 0.3.8: a board sweep now always glides all the way to its target and eases out there instead of stopping dead at the edge of the comfort zone, and a paused or interrupted sweep can never snap to its end when the song resumes.\n\n0.3.8 polishes game feel: a struck note keeps sinking into the piano instead of vanishing on tap, the board glide sweeps smoothly to the next notes with no lurch at the start or end, and hit sparks stay in a tight column right at the border between the falling notes and the piano instead of spreading over the screen.\n\nThe built-in folder explorer lists a folder you pick once, so you can open files without leaving the app. Browsing is read-only: no delete, rename or move.\n\nSigned with the tengok key (certificate SHA-256 439CF7177600DCB04E32A197AD0BC1FD084B78DC329224201EC2A1845E9B8EE9).\nSHA-256 of the APK is in the attached .sha256 file.\n"
